From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: qcom-hv-haptics: build with tracing enabled

ROCKNIX's SM8550 haptics driver (1000-add-qcom-haptics-driver.patch) still
uses the two-argument __assign_str() that Linux 6.10 removed. ROCKNIX builds
with CONFIG_FTRACE off, so the trace event compiles away; SteamOS needs
tracefs (steamos.config), which exposes it. Also passes the missing rc to a
dev_err() format.

Same fix as MaSi's 1001-qcom-haptics-trace-7.0.patch
(external-and-mods/kernel/patches/masi), regenerated for ROCKNIX 20260801.
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
--- a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
@@ -5776,7 +5776,7 @@
 
 	rc = haptics_enable_hpwr_vreg(chip, false);
 	if (rc < 0)
-		dev_err(chip->dev, "disable hpwr_vreg failed, rc=%d\n");
+		dev_err(chip->dev, "disable hpwr_vreg failed, rc=%d\n", rc);
 
 	return count;
 }
diff --git a/include/trace/events/qcom_haptics.h b/include/trace/events/qcom_haptics.h
--- a/include/trace/events/qcom_haptics.h
+++ b/include/trace/events/qcom_haptics.h
@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@
 	),
 
 	TP_fast_assign(
-		__assign_str(id_name, name);
+		__assign_str(id_name);
 		__entry->msb = msb;
 		__entry->lsb = lsb;
 	),
